<p>FRNP supports the small business objectives of the Department of Energy and recognizes that diversity in subcontracting provides a vital link to the local community, strengthens the economy and represents best business practices. FRNP will subcontract more than 30% of the work with 50% going to small businesses.</p>

<h1>Interested?</h1>

<p>Suppliers interested in doing business with FRNP must complete a “<a href="https://fourriversnuclearpartnership.files.wordpress.com/2017/11/supplier-data-sheet.pdf" rel="noopener" target="_blank" title="Supplier Data Sheet">Supplier Data Sheet</a>”. The form, along with any relevant information regarding your Company’s capabilities, should be forwarded to: <a href="mailto:FRNPProcurement@pad.pppo.gov">FRNPProcurement@pad.pppo.gov</a>.</p>

<p>Four Rivers NP procurement activities are conducted in a manner that fosters the highest degree of ethical conduct and public trust. Any conflict of interest or even the appearance of a conflict of interest will be avoided or mitigated. Please review the brochure entitled “<a href="https://fourriversnuclearpartnership.files.wordpress.com/2017/11/business-conduct-guidelines.pdf" rel="noopener" target="_blank" title="Business Conduct Guidelines">Business Conduct Guidelines</a>” for FRNP’s procurement ethics policy.</p>

